KZ3 patch 2185 (RSX pass 163): LD_WB_DEFER=1, the deferred guest write-back (default OFF; unset = the old synchronous
paths, no new work beyond a few not-taken branches). New libs/video/rsx_wb_defer.h (GPU-free pending-store queue: readback
slot ownership, oldest-first drain with ONE wait on the newest fence, overlap queries, verify compare, [wb-defer] line,
published range snapshot; host test tools/smoke/test_wb_defer.sh).
- Store points (rsx_live_draw.c, ld_writeback_batch(.., defer_ok)): the NV0039 scene copy batch and the 0x4A-release batch of
  main surfaces (LD_WB_DEFER_LABEL, default 0x4A, set by cellGcmSys around before_guest_sync) record the GPU copy into a
  readback slot, submit with ld_submit_nowait (ld_oq_close first, as ld_flush does) and queue {fence, slot, destination,
  frozen geometry, generation, seq}. The surface's gv_gpu_dirty clears at the submit (as the synchronous store clears it).
  Nothing submitted (no fence advance) = this chunk keeps today's synchronous store, after draining the older entries.
- The idx0 row copy of nv0039_copy (local 0x1300000 -> main 0x01310400) is queued too when a pending store covers its source
  (rsx_live_draw_wbd_defer_move, nv0039_rows callback); the rest of nv0039_copy runs as before.
- ONE drain, gcm_walker_user_command before cellGcmQueueUserCommand (0xEB00): wait the newest fence once, then every store
  oldest-first (idx0's move after its source surface). Readers drain first: guest_ptr (every renderer read of guest bytes),
  ld_tsl_prologue and vertex_texture_srv_slot (before their dirty-page checks), nv0039_copy source and destination, the NV3089
  engine source read, any synchronous write-back batch (reason other), the flip. Readback slots stay taken until their store
  ran; no free slots = forced drain (reason slot); queue full = drain (reason full).
- Deferred stores redo the store's side effects at the drain (ld_td_mark, ld_pwd_note_writeback, ld_wbp_store, guest-validate
  baseline, gv_pending when the surface was drawn since the copy) only while the surface record is still the same one.
- LD_WB_DEFER_VERIFY=1: also reads each slot at the original point (GPU wait, as today) into a shadow, compares it with the
  deferred conversion at the drain and counts [wb-defer] mismatches (also: moved rows differing from their source).
- Not deferred: FIFO capture runs, LD_WRITEBACK_BATCH=0, every sync point but the labelled release.
- [wb-defer] line every LD_WB_READ_N (default 100) flips: pending_max, pushes, drains, waits, wait_ms, stores, aborted,
  forced drains by reason, verified, mismatches, bytes_bad, plus the first mismatching (surface, offset) and the racy counters
  spu_gets_of_pending / spu_writes_into_pending (SPU GET hook now also installed with LD_WB_DEFER).
- Non-Windows stubs and the two host-test stub files carry the new rsx_live_draw_wbd_* symbols.

