+/* ===========================================================================
+ * Patch 2185 (RSX pass 163): LD_WB_DEFER=1 -- deferred guest write-back (default OFF; unset = the loops above unchanged).
+ * The store points (the NV0039 scene copy, the 0x4A release's main surfaces) record their GPU copy into a readback slot and
+ * submit without a wait; the pending entry {fence, slot, destination, geometry, seq} waits in g_wbd (rsx_wb_defer.h). ONE
+ * drain (gcm_walker_user_command, before 0xEB00 is queued) waits the newest fence and stores every entry oldest-first.
+ * Readers of those guest bytes drain first: guest_ptr (all renderer reads), the texture binds (before their dirty-page
+ * checks), NV0039 copies and the NV3089 source read (rsx_live_draw_wbd_touch), the flip. Slots are not reused before
+ * their store ran (forced drain, reason slot). LD_WB_DEFER_VERIFY=1 also reads each slot at the original point (GPU wait,
+ * as today) into a shadow and compares it with the deferred conversion at the drain: [wb-defer] mismatches=N, must be 0.
+ * LD_WB_DEFER_LABEL (default 0x4A) = the label whose release defers the main surfaces. Not deferred (always synchronous):
+ * FIFO capture runs (LD_FIFO_CAPTURE), LD_WRITEBACK_BATCH=0, every other sync point. ASSUMPTION: the SPU post chain
+ * starts only from the 0xEB00 handler (the RE notes pass 188); LD_WB_HASH=1 A/B against the baseline checks it.
